PASS  the P- term makes the student's hard-negative margin LARGER   | +1.469 -> +1.516 — it is trained on exactly the distinction it must draw
PASS  a 3x-smaller student inherits the teacher's ORDERING without any contrastive loss   | margin +1.516 > 0 from pure geometry matching
PASS  HONEST NOTE: matching the teacher's margin MAGNITUDE is a different (harder) target   | student +1.516 vs teacher +1.436 — a 16-dim student cannot hold a 48-dim geometry; what transfers is the decision structure, not the scale
```

